docs/book/src/concepts/agent-loop.md:101:`RunResultStreaming::new(stream).collect().await?` drains every event, returning a `RunResult` whose `final_output: String` is the concatenated text of the *last* `MessageOutput` assistant message, alongside the full `events` vector and aggregated `usage`. A terminal `RunFailed` surfaces as `Err(RunError)`. For structured output, use `collect_typed::<T>()` instead. A run that ends with `RunDeferred` has no completed answer. For such a run, `collect` returns a `RunResult` with `StopReason::Deferred { calls }` in `stop_reason`. Its `final_output` can be non-empty: it keeps the text of an earlier `MessageOutput`, for example "I will ask for approval". That text is not a completed answer. Check `stop_reason` before you use `final_output`. Do not expect an empty string. `collect_typed` returns `AgentError::Incomplete`. A run that ends with `RunStopped` also has no completed answer. For such a run, `collect` returns `StopReason::Stopped { reason }` in `stop_reason`, and `collect_typed` returns `AgentError::Incomplete`. `RunResult.stop_reason` is `StopReason::Completed` for a run that finished.

